      "message": "This is redundant.\n\n----\n\nSince `kMaxRetry` is already defined as an `inline constexpr int` in `cli.h`, creating local aliases like `constexpr int kRetries \u003d kMaxRetry;` inside the functions is completely redundant. In fact, you already use `kMaxRetry` directly inside `ExecuteCommand` further down in the file!\n\nYou can safely remove these local constant re-declarations and just use `kMaxRetry` directly in the loops.\n\nHere are the two places in `util/focaltech/cli.cc` you should clean up:\n\n**1. In `CheckEcBuildVersion`:**\n\n*Remove:*\n\n```cpp\n  constexpr int kRetries \u003d kMaxRetry;\n  std::string build_info;\n\n  for (int attempt \u003d 1; attempt \u003c\u003d kRetries; ++attempt) {\n\n```\n\n*Replace with:*\n\n```cpp\n  std::string build_info;\n\n  for (int attempt \u003d 1; attempt \u003c\u003d kMaxRetry; ++attempt) {\n\n```\n\n**2. In `SwitchMcuMode`:**\n\n*Remove:*\n\n```cpp\n  // Attempt the switch with retries; device loss indicates success\n  constexpr int kMaxSwitchRetries \u003d kMaxRetry;\n  bool device_lost \u003d false;\n\n  for (int attempt \u003d 1; attempt \u003c\u003d kMaxSwitchRetries; ++attempt) {\n\n```\n\n*Replace with:*\n\n```cpp\n  // Attempt the switch with retries; device loss indicates success\n  bool device_lost \u003d false;\n\n  for (int attempt \u003d 1; attempt \u003c\u003d kMaxRetry; ++attempt) {\n\n```",
