      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `libusb_transport.cc`, the logic that identifies the Focal device is nested in a way that requires some mental gymnastics to read:\n\n**The issue:**\n\n```c\n    if (is_boot || is_rom || is_ec) {\n      if (is_ec) {\n        const bool valid_fp \u003d (pid \u003d\u003d kFocalEcPidTest) ||\n                              (pid \u003d\u003d kFocalEcPid9865) ||\n                              (pid \u003d\u003d kFocalEcPid9869);\n        if (!valid_fp) {\n          FT_LOGI(\"Found Google device {:04x}:{:04x}, but not Focal. Skipping.\",\n                  vid, pid);\n          continue;\n        }\n      }\n      return dev;\n    }\n\n```\n\n**The Simplification:** You can eliminate the nesting by checking the simplest states first and returning early.\n\n*Refactored:*\n\n```c\n    if (is_boot || is_rom) {\n      return dev;\n    }\n    \n    if (is_ec) {\n      const bool valid_fp \u003d (pid \u003d\u003d kFocalEcPidTest) ||\n                            (pid \u003d\u003d kFocalEcPid9865) ||\n                            (pid \u003d\u003d kFocalEcPid9869);\n      if (valid_fp) {\n        return dev;\n      }\n      FT_LOGI(\"Found Google device {:04x}:{:04x}, but not Focal. Skipping.\", vid, pid);\n    }\n\n```\n\nThis reads linearly, clearly isolating the Google/EC VID special case from the dedicated ROM/Boot VIDs.",
