      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback. Verify that it is correct:\n\n----\n\nIn `updater.cc`, `DownloadBin` allocates a `write_buffer` padded to the nearest 4096-byte page boundary, initializes it with `0xFF`, and copies the entire firmware into it.\n\n**The issue:** You only ever iterate over the exact `file_len`, padding the *very last* chunk to a 4-byte boundary. The only time the code explicitly uses `write_buffer.data()` is at the very end to write the 4KB config page. But because the firmware is much larger than 4KB, the first 4KB of `write_buffer` is *identical* to the first 4KB of the original `buffer`. The padded allocation is completely unused\\!\n\n**The Simplification:** Delete `write_buffer` entirely and just use the original `buffer` vector.\n\n*Remove this:*\n\n```c\n  size_t padded_buffer_size \u003d total_frame * kFocalConfigSize;\n  // 0xFF is the initial value of flash.\n  constexpr uint8_t kFlashInitValue \u003d 0xFF;\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e write_buffer(padded_buffer_size, kFlashInitValue);\n  std::memcpy(write_buffer.data(), buffer.data(), file_len);\n\n  uint8_t* p \u003d write_buffer.data();\n\n```\n\n*Replace with this:*\n\n```c\n  // Point directly to the original file buffer\n  const uint8_t* p \u003d buffer.data(); \n\n```\n\nThen, at the very end of the function where the config page is written, update the reference to use `buffer`:\n\n```c\n  if (target_addr \u003d\u003d kFocalBootCfgAddr || target_addr \u003d\u003d kFocalRomCfgAddr) {\n    FT_LOGI(\"Write config page\");\n    auto page_res \u003d DownloadPage(device, target_addr, kFocalConfigSize,\n                                   {buffer.data(), kFocalConfigSize}); // \u003c-- Changed to buffer.data()\n    // ...\n\n```\n\nThis saves \\~2MB of heap allocation and an unnecessary `memcpy` of the entire firmware\\!",
