      "message": "Since we\u0027re using C++, we don\u0027t need the `Ft` prefix. We can use namespaces. Here are Gemini instructions to rename functions and use the `focaltech` namespace:\n\n----\n\n### Step 1: Rename Types and Enums\n\nTo fully embrace the C++ namespace, strip the `Ft` prefix from your core data types across all headers (`ft_util.h`, `usb_device.h`, `updater.h`, `ft_scsi.h`) and update their references in the `.cc` files:\n\n* `FtError` ➔ **`Error`**\n* `FtDeviceMode` ➔ **`DeviceMode`**\n* `FtDeviceInfo` ➔ **`DeviceInfo`**\n* `FtFlashWpArea` ➔ **`FlashWpArea`**\n* `FtConfigPage` ➔ **`ConfigPage`**\n* `FtCmdFormat` ➔ **`CmdFormat`**\n\n### Step 2: Rename the Functions\n\nUpdate these function signatures in the headers (`cli.h`, `updater.h`) and their implementations/callers in the `.cc` files:\n\n* `DeviceInit` ➔ **`InitDevice`**\n* `IsEcBinHasConfigPage` ➔ **`HasValidConfigPage`**\n* `FtBackToRomBoot` ➔ **`ReturnToRomBoot`**\n* `FtMcuReset` ➔ **`ResetMcu`**\n* `FtGetFlashProtect` ➔ **`GetFlashProtection`**\n* `FtSetFlashProtect` ➔ **`SetFlashProtection`**\n* `FtErasePage` ➔ **`ErasePage`**\n* `FtDownloadPage` ➔ **`DownloadPage`**\n* `FtDownloadBin` ➔ **`DownloadBin`**\n* `FtVerifyData` ➔ **`VerifyData`**\n* `FtGetBootVersion` ➔ **`GetBootVersion`**\n* *(Note: The math helper `FtDivRoundUp` in `ft_util.h` should also become just `DivRoundUp`)*\n\n### Step 3: Wrap Headers and Source Files in `namespace focaltech`\n\nFor the following files, place `namespace focaltech {` right after your `#include` directives, and `}  // namespace focaltech` at the very bottom of the file.\n\n**Headers:**\n\n* `cli.h`\n* `ft_help.h`\n* `ft_log.h` *(Note: you already have `namespace ft_log` here, you can nest it or rename it to `namespace focaltech::log`)*\n* `ft_scsi.h`\n* `ft_util.h`\n* `updater.h`\n* `usb_device.h`\n* `usb_transport.h`\n\n**Source Files:**\n\n* `cli.cc`\n* `ft_scsi.cc`\n* `updater.cc`\n\n*(Note: `libusb_transport.h/cc` and `test_utils.h` are already in the `focaltech` namespace, so you don\u0027t need to change their namespace boundaries).*\n\n### Step 4: Update `main.cc`\n\nBecause `main()` must remain in the global namespace, you will need to explicitly use the `focaltech::` prefix for the types and functions you just moved.\n\nReplace the bottom half of your `main.cc` with this:\n\n```cpp\n  // 1. Parse Inputs (Logic now lives in cli.cc)\n  auto config \u003d focaltech::ParseArguments(args);\n  if (!config) return EXIT_FAILURE;\n\n  // 2. Create Hardware Connection\n  auto transport \u003d focaltech::LibusbTransport::Create();\n  if (!transport) {\n    FT_LOGE(\"Failed to open USB device.\");\n    return EXIT_FAILURE;\n  }\n\n  // 3. Inject hardware into domain object\n  focaltech::UsbDevice usb_device(std::make_unique\u003cfocaltech::LibusbTransport\u003e(\n      std::move(transport.value())));\n\n  focaltech::DeviceInfo info;\n  if (auto init_res \u003d focaltech::InitDevice(usb_device.device_id(), info); !init_res) {\n    FT_LOGE(\"Cannot find Focal device\");\n    return EXIT_FAILURE;\n  }\n\n  // 4. Execute\n  if (auto exec_res \u003d focaltech::ExecuteCommand(config.value(), usb_device, info);\n      !exec_res) {\n    FT_LOGE(\"Command failed\");\n    return EXIT_FAILURE;\n  }\n  return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n\n```\n\n### Step 5: Wrap the Tests (Option 1)\n\nTo comply with the Google C++ Style Guide while avoiding `focaltech::` boilerplate in your tests, wrap all of your test files inside the `focaltech` namespace.\n\nApply this structure to `cli_test.cc`, `updater_test.cc`, `ft_scsi_test.cc`, `ft_util_test.cc`, `usb_device_test.cc`, and `ft_help_test.cc`:\n\n```cpp\n/* Copyright ... */\n\n#include \"...\" // Your includes\n#include \u003cgtest/gtest.h\u003e\n\nnamespace focaltech {\n\nnamespace {\n// Your test helpers, constants, and fake classes go here\n} // namespace\n\n// Your TEST() macros go here. \n// Because they are inside namespace focaltech, they can call InitDevice(), \n// Error, and ReturnToRomBoot() directly without prefixes!\nTEST(UpdaterTest, UpdateFw_SuccessBootloaderMode) {\n  // ...\n}\n\n}  // namespace focaltech\n\n```\n\n*(Note: In `updater_test.cc` and `ft_scsi_test.cc`, you can now remove lines like `using ::focaltech::testing::BuildValidCsw;` because being inside the `focaltech` namespace gives you direct access to the `testing` inner namespace!)*",
