      "message": "### The Issue: `DeviceInfo` is a Mutable Data Bag\n\nIn `usb_device.h`, you have this struct:\n\n```cpp\nstruct DeviceInfo {\n  DeviceMode current_mode \u003d DeviceMode::kUnknown;\n  DeviceMode next_mode \u003d DeviceMode::kUnknown;\n  std::string_view ec_bin;\n};\n\n```\n\n1. `next_mode` is **100% dead code**. It is never read or written anywhere in the codebase.\n2. `ec_bin` is already securely held inside `AppConfig`! You copy it over in `ExecuteCommand` just to pass it to `UpdateFw`.\n3. Because of this struct, `InitDevice` requires an out-parameter (`InitDevice(usb.device_id(), info)`), which is less idiomatic than simply returning a value.\n\n### The Fix: Make the Data Flow Functional\n\n**1. Delete the struct entirely**\nOpen `util/focaltech/usb_device.h` and simply delete the `DeviceInfo` struct.\n\n**2. Turn `InitDevice` into `GetDeviceMode**`\nIn `cli.h` and `cli.cc`, replace `InitDevice` with a function that strictly evaluates the USB IDs and returns the mode:\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cDeviceMode, Error\u003e GetDeviceMode(const UsbDeviceId\u0026 details) {\n  switch (details.vid) {\n    case kFocalRomVid:\n      return DeviceMode::kRom;\n    case kFocalBootVid:\n      return DeviceMode::kBoot;\n    case kFocalEcVid:\n      return (details.pid \u003d\u003d kFocalEcPidTest) ? DeviceMode::kTest : DeviceMode::kEc;\n    default:\n      FT_LOGE(\"Unrecognized Focal device.\");\n      return std::unexpected(Error::kNoSuchDevice);\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n*(Look at how much cleaner that `switch` statement is without all the `break`s and `info.current_mode \u003d ...` assignments!)*\n\n**3. Update `ExecuteCommand` to take the mode directly**\nIn `cli.h` and `cli.cc`, update the signature to accept `DeviceMode current_mode` instead of the struct.\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, Error\u003e ExecuteCommand(const AppConfig\u0026 config,\n                                          UsbDevice\u0026 usb_device,\n                                          DeviceMode current_mode) {\n// ...\n\n```\n\nInside the `Command::kUpdate` switch case, you no longer need to copy the `ec_bin` string. Just pass it directly to `UpdateFw`:\n\n```cpp\n    case Command::kUpdate:\n      FT_LOGI(\"Updating firmware...\");\n      if (config.ec_bin.empty()) {\n        FT_LOGE(\"No firmware file specified\");\n        return std::unexpected(Error::kParameterError);\n      }\n      \n      for (int attempt \u003d 1; attempt \u003c\u003d kMaxRetry; ++attempt) {\n        // Pass config.ec_bin and current_mode directly!\n        if (auto res \u003d UpdateFw(usb_device, config.ec_bin, current_mode); res) {\n          FT_LOGI(\"Firmware update successful\");\n          return {};\n        }\n// ...\n\n```\n\n**4. Update `UpdateFw` to accept the isolated variables**\nIn `updater.h` and `updater.cc`, change the signature from `DeviceInfo\u0026 info` to the individual required variables:\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, Error\u003e UpdateFw(const UsbDevice\u0026 device,\n                                    std::string_view ec_bin,\n                                    DeviceMode current_mode) {\n// ...\n\n```\n\n*(You will just need to replace the couple of references to `info.ec_bin` with `ec_bin`, and `info.current_mode` with `current_mode` inside the function).*\n\n**5. Clean up `main.cc**`\nFinally, your entry point becomes incredibly linear and functional, with no mutable out-parameters!\n\n```cpp\n  // 3. Inject hardware into domain object\n  focaltech::UsbDevice usb_device(std::make_unique\u003cfocaltech::LibusbTransport\u003e(\n      std::move(transport.value())));\n\n  // Get the mode directly\n  auto mode_res \u003d focaltech::GetDeviceMode(usb_device.device_id());\n  if (!mode_res) {\n    FT_LOGE(\"Cannot find Focal device\");\n    return EXIT_FAILURE;\n  }\n\n  // 4. Execute using the resolved mode\n  if (auto exec_res \u003d focaltech::ExecuteCommand(config.value(), usb_device, *mode_res);\n      !exec_res) {\n    FT_LOGE(\"Command failed\");\n    return EXIT_FAILURE;\n  }\n\n```\n\nThis drastically simplifies the data architecture of the tool. State now flows strictly downward (Config ➔ Mode ➔ Execute ➔ Update), effectively wiping out the last remaining \"C-style\" state-bag pattern from the migration!",
